> w(acc: f32, i: u32 in 0..255) = atomic_add_shared(acc, f32(i) * 0.25)
> cost w
cost of w under gt1030: 28.25 (3 operations, shared subterms counted once)
  conv             1 x 3     = 3
  fmul             1 x 1     = 1
  atomic_shared_f   1 x 24.25 = 24.25
> intatomic w
intatomic w under gt1030: a shared float atomic add of 0.25f32(i), at most 1024 into one cell
  the float add costs 24.25, an integer one 6.625
  the addend is k 2^-2 with |k| <= 255, exactly: every leaf is an integer or a binary constant, the
  operations keep the grid, and no f32 value on the way needs more than 24 bits, so none rounds
  the sum of 1024 of them is at most 261120 2^-2: it fits 32 bits (261120 < 2^31), so the integer sum is the exact sum
  the float sum would be exact too (it stays within 24 bits): the two agree bit for bit, in every order
  the integer addend: i32(i)
  -> atomic_add_shared(acc, i32(i)): addend and atomic cost 6.625 against 28.25 (-76.5%)
     the cell is an i32 holding the sum times 2^2; every other access of it changes too: a store of v
     stores i32(v * 2^2), a read is f32(cell) * 2^-2 (a conversion and a multiply: 4 a read)
  defined w_ia: the atomic's old value read back as a float
> cost w_ia
cost of w_ia under gt1030: 10.625 (3 operations, shared subterms counted once)
  conv             1 x 3     = 3
  fmul             1 x 1     = 1
  atomic_shared    1 x 6.625 = 6.625
> intatomic w count 100000000
intatomic w under gt1030: a shared float atomic add of 0.25f32(i), at most 100000000 into one cell
  the float add costs 24.25, an integer one 6.625
  the addend is k 2^-2 with |k| <= 255, exactly: every leaf is an integer or a binary constant, the
  operations keep the grid, and no f32 value on the way needs more than 24 bits, so none rounds
  -> not rewritten: 100000000 addends of up to 255 can reach 25500000000, past 2^31 - 1; fewer adds (`count N`) or a narrower range
> wt(acc: f32, x: f32 in 0..1) = atomic_add_shared(acc, x)
> intatomic wt
intatomic wt under gt1030: a shared float atomic add of x, at most 1024 into one cell
  the float add costs 24.25, an integer one 6.625
  no exact fixed point: x is not on a binary grid (only integers, binary constants, + - * and powers of two keep one)
  -> not rewritten: `tol T` allows a rounded scaling (T: absolute error on the sum)
> intatomic wt tol 1e-3
intatomic wt under gt1030: a shared float atomic add of x, at most 1024 into one cell
  the float add costs 24.25, an integer one 6.625
  no exact fixed point: x is not on a binary grid (only integers, binary constants, + - * and powers of two keep one)
  |addend| <= 1: scaled by 2^20 (exact; below 2^22, so + 0.5 and floor are exact too) and rounded to nearest
  each is off by at most 2^-21, 1024 of them by 0.000488281; the sum fits 32 bits
  the integer addend: i32(floor(1048576x + 0.5))
  -> atomic_add_shared(acc, i32(floor(1048576x + 0.5))): addend and atomic cost 13.625 against 24.25 (-43.8%)
     the cell is an i32 holding the sum times 2^20; every other access of it changes too: a store of v
     stores i32(v * 2^20), a read is f32(cell) * 2^-20 (a conversion and a multiply: 4 a read)
  defined wt_ia: the atomic's old value read back as a float
> wg(acc: f32, i: u32 in 0..255) = atomic_add(acc, f32(i))
> intatomic wg
intatomic wg under gt1030: a global float atomic add of f32(i), at most 1024 into one cell
  the float add costs 138.75, an integer one 50
  the addend is k 2^0 with |k| <= 255, exactly: every leaf is an integer or a binary constant, the
  operations keep the grid, and no f32 value on the way needs more than 24 bits, so none rounds
  the sum of 1024 of them is at most 261120 2^0: it fits 32 bits (261120 < 2^31), so the integer sum is the exact sum
  the float sum would be exact too (it stays within 24 bits): the two agree bit for bit, in every order
  the integer addend: i32(i)
