> banks row
banks under gt1030: 32 banks of 4 bytes, a warp of 32 lanes, 4-byte elements; a shared load 3, each further address on a bank +4
  row = 32r + lane
    lane parameter lane; conflict degree 1: index = 1 lane + b: two lanes share a bank when 32 divides 1 (l - l'), that is when 32 divides l - l', so 32 gcd(1, 32) / 32 = 1 lane a bank; all 32 cases enumerated too
    price 3
  array size taken as 1024 (the largest index 1023, in whole rows of 32; `size N` to say)
  -> not rewritten: no swizzle (row xored or added into the bank bits, a padded row) makes the 1 access cheaper than 3 under gt1030
> banks col
banks under gt1030: 32 banks of 4 bytes, a warp of 32 lanes, 4-byte elements; a shared load 3, each further address on a bank +4
  col = 32lane + c
    lane parameter lane; conflict degree 32: index = 32 lane + b: two lanes share a bank when 32 divides 32 (l - l'), that is when 1 divides l - l', so 32 gcd(32, 32) / 32 = 32 lanes a bank; all 32 cases enumerated too
    price 127
  array size taken as 1024 (the largest index 1023, in whole rows of 32; `size N` to say)
  -> swizzle every index i of the array: i + (i >> 5)
     it is strictly increasing (i + 1 lands after i), so no two indices meet; the array grows to 1055 elements: every index enumerated
     col_sw = t1 + (t1 >> 5) where t1 = 32lane + c
       conflict degree 1 (index = 33 lane + b: two lanes share a bank when 32 divides 33 (l - l'), that is when 32 divides l - l', so 32 gcd(33, 32) / 32 = 1 lane a bank; all 32 cases enumerated too): price 3 + 2 for the swizzle
     total 5 against 127 (-96.1%); every access of the array takes the swizzle, reads and writes alike
