  ucas: intatomic w
intatomic w under gt1030: a shared float atomic add of 0.25f32(i), at most 1024 into one cell
  the float add costs 24.25, an integer one 6.625
  the addend is k 2^-2 with |k| <= 255, exactly: every leaf is an integer or a binary constant, the
  operations keep the grid, and no f32 value on the way needs more than 24 bits, so none rounds
  the sum of 1024 of them is at most 261120 2^-2: it fits 32 bits (261120 < 2^31), so the integer sum is the exact sum
  the float sum would be exact too (it stays within 24 bits): the two agree bit for bit, in every order
  the integer addend: i32(i)
  -> atomic_add_shared(acc, i32(i)): addend and atomic cost 6.625 against 28.25 (-76.5%)
     the cell is an i32 holding the sum times 2^2; every other access of it changes too: a store of v
     stores i32(v * 2^2), a read is f32(cell) * 2^-2 (a conversion and a multiply: 4 a read)
  defined w_ia: the atomic's old value read back as a float
